; revised 2026-09-14 (r2) per the\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:37:## §7.1 Stance: a continuation is a value, not a session\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:51:| Role | Does | Holds |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:53:| **Emitter** | lifts a parked configuration into a UCF value and appends it to a medium | nothing, once appended |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:54:| **Carrier** | any stream, file, DHT, or socket that moves the value; sees opaque data | nothing |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:55:| **Resumer** | reads the value, satisfies its declared context, obtains custody, lowers, runs | custody, for the duration of a lease |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:60:**a UCF value on a stream is not a claim**: a stream has no privileged reader\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:76:## §7.2 Vocabulary and envelope\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:131:## §7.3 Code identity — content-addressed semantic profiles (blocker 5)\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:133:### 7.3.1 The problem restated as data\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:139:### 7.3.2 The canonical instruction vector and its address\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:160:**Input.** The vector is computed from a well-formed batch (§2.6) by first\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:172:**The vector.** With the resolution applied, the canonical instruction\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:215:**The address** is `(dao.jing/segment-key vector)` — a\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:223:**What equal addresses do and do not mean.** Two segments address equally\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:224:**iff** their loader-resolved interpretations are equal; this includes\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:239:### 7.3.3 The contract stamp\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:246:**complete execution contract**: the stamp names one published revision of\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:272:**per stamp revision**: lookup is `(get-in index [stamp address])`, and the\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:276:### 7.3.4 References to code inside a continuation\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:284:**The addressed object is the vector.** `dao.jing` materializes the exact\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:293:**projection path** converts the vector to loadable datoms deterministically\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:324:**The address index is additive; local-id immutability stands.** The §3.1\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:336:**The continuation's own identity and the occurrence.** `:yin.k/id` is the\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:339:**id-less body**; a reader reconstructs the envelope with\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:350:## §7.4 Safepoints — where a canonical configuration exists (blocker 1)\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:352:### 7.4.1 Only safepoints lift, and the table is the machine's\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:367:| Safepoint kind | Raised by | Canonical resume pc | Stack in frame (St) | Accumulator on resume |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:369:| explicit park | `:park` | `pc+1` | St at park | the resume value |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:370:| blocked read | `:stream-next` → `blocked` | `pc+1` | St (cursor ref was in `val`) | the read value; `nil` on `end`, `:dao.stream/gap` on gap |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:371:| blocked write | `:stream-put` → `full` | `pc+1` | St minus the popped target ref | the written value, on retry `ok` |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:372:| FFI call, sent | `:ffi-call` → `:dao.stream/ok` | `pc+1` | St minus the popped args | the correlated response's `ok` value; its `error` raises |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:373:| FFI call, retained | `:ffi-call` → `:dao.stream/full` | `pc+1` | St minus the popped args | as sent, once the request is appended and the response correlates |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:374:| effectful call | `:call`/`:tailcall` whose operator yields a blocking effect (`require`, stream-module functions, effect handlers) | `pc+1` | St minus the popped operator and args | the effect's resume value, per its kind as above |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:375:| halt | `:halt`, `:return` with empty K | — | — | not resumable; a `:yin.k/type :yin.k/result` travels instead |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:403:**Quiescence.** The migration unit is one task: the whole blocked machine\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:408:### 7.4.2 Safepoint maps for foreign engines: static facts only\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:465:### 7.4.3 The pending wait travels as data — complete, and resumable elsewhere\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:539:## §7.5 Recursive portable encoding (blocker 2)\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:541:### 7.5.1 A disjoint tagged grammar\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:557:| Encoded form | Tag | Contents | Decodes to |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:559:| scalars: nil, boolean, number, string, keyword, symbol | — | themselves (never a map; cannot forge a marker) | themselves |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:560:| vector, list, set | — | same shape, elements recursively encoded (never a map) | same shape, elements decoded |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:561:| literal map | `:yin.k/literal` | `:yin.k/entries [k₁ v₁ k₂ v₂ …]`, keys and values recursively encoded | the map, keys and values decoded |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:562:| closure | `:yin.k/closure` | `:yin.k/segment addr :yin.k/entry pc :yin.k/params […] :yin.k/env {encoded}` | `{:type :closure …}` (§2.4) |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:563:| reified continuation | `:yin.k/frame` | a nested frame (§7.4.1), recursively | `{:type :reified-continuation …}` |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:564:| parked continuation | `:yin.k/frame` | a nested frame plus `:yin.k/parked-id` | `{:type :parked-continuation …}` |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:565:| primitive | `:yin.k/primitive` | `:yin.k/name sym` | the named function, after profile check (§7.5.2) |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:566:| stream reference | `:yin.k/stream` | `:dao.stream/identity … :dao.stream/descriptor …` | an attached handle, under a fresh store key |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:567:| cursor reference | `:yin.k/cursor-ref` | `:yin.k/cell cell-id` | a store cursor entry for that cell, §7.5.3 |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:568:| shared subvalue | `:yin.k/ref` | `:yin.k/id addr` | the table entry at `addr`, §7.5.3 |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:569:| anything else | — | — | **refused**: `:yin.k/non-portable` |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:584:**Decoding validates, independent of hashing.** A hash check confirms what\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:595:### 7.5.2 Primitives: a name is a binding, not a meaning\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:650:### 7.5.3 Sharing, cells, and cycles\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:652:**The value table.** A configuration is a DAG, not a tree: a closure's\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:681:**Cursor cells.** A cursor is *observable state with aliasing*: two distinct\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:690:**logical cursor cells** separately from position content:\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:717:### 7.5.4 Failure is total and names its place\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:731:| :cyclic | :in-memory-handle | :non-canonicalizable | :foreign-parked-ref`\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:740:## §7.6 Dependency closure and context (blocker 3)\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:742:### 7.6.1 Declared, not hand-written — and discovered conservatively\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:812:### 7.6.2 The store slice, restored as an isolated store\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:830:**There is no merge.** The first draft said, in two places, both that the\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:849:### 7.6.3 The migration unit is one task\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:881:### 7.6.4 Modules\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:894:### 7.6.5 The satisfaction check\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:922:## §7.7 Ownership arbitration — custody as a lease over datoms (blocker 4)\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:924:### 7.7.1 The race, named\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:939:### 7.7.2 Custody facts, and their dispatch keys\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:948:| Fact | Dispatch | Author | Required keys |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:950:| offer | `:yin.k/custody :yin.k/offered` | emitter | `:yin.k/occurrence`, `:yin.k/id` (this snapshot variant), `:yin.k/policy`, `:yin.k/medium` (the carrier identity) |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:951:| checkpoint done | `:yin.k/custody :yin.k/resumed` | holder | `:yin.k/occurrence`, `:dao.lease/lease`, `:yin.k/result` — the address of the successor's occurrence value or of a `:yin.k/result` |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:965:**only grantor-authored facts establish terms.**\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:973:### 7.7.3 The authority: what the grantor possesses\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:985:**The possessed resource is the occurrence's execution ledger**: the set of\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:988:**admission epoch** (§7.7.5). The **grantor is the boundary that transacts\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1019:### 7.7.4 The exporting state: fencing the source before publication\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1059:**Failure recovery and idempotent retry.** If publication fails — a full\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1069:### 7.7.5 Fencing effects: epochs, operation ids, and what exactly-once costs\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1083:**Authority epochs, checked atomically with commitment.** The occurrence's\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1094:**Stable operation ids, and durable dedup.** Every fenced effect carries\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1106:**Where the stamp rides.** Program values are program data; UCF never\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1108:**fenced writer** the composition wires: a writer that wraps each appended\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1119:**Durable completion of a checkpoint.** Publication of a successor is not\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1133:**Partition policy, stated honestly.** A fenced consumer that cannot reach\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1149:### 7.7.6 Successors and chains\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1165:### 7.7.7 Restart\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1175:## §7.8 Lifecycle: lift on park, lower on resume\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1177:**Lift** (emitter side; composition-driven, never automatic on every park):\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1200:**Lower** (resumer side):\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1237:## §7.9 Outcome algebra\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1242:| `:yin.k/status` | Raised by | Carries |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1244:| `:yin.k/ok` | any | the value, or the lowered VM |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1245:| `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint` | lift | `:yin.k/segment`, `:yin.k/pc` |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1246:| `:yin.k/not-quiescent` | lift | the ready-queue depth |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1247:| `:yin.k/non-portable` | lift | `:yin.k/path`, `:yin.k/kind`, `:yin.k/hint` — kinds at §7.5.4, cycles included as `:kind :cyclic` |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1248:| `:yin.k/profile-mismatch` | lower | `:yin.k/contract` expected and found |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1249:| `:yin.k/hash-mismatch` | lower | the address claimed and the address computed |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1250:| `:yin.k/undecodable` | lower | `:yin.k/path`, the structural defect — malformed markers, missing or cyclic refs, malformed-but-correctly-hashed bodies |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1251:| `:yin.k/unsatisfied` | lower | `:yin.k/missing`, `:yin.k/discovery` — includes attachment failures, cursor profiles, and an unreachable arbitration medium |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1252:| `:yin.k/awaiting-grant` | lower | `:yin.k/occurrence`, the proposal — a step status while a proposal is unanswered, bounded by nothing (`dao.lease.md`) |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1253:| `:yin.k/not-holder` | lower | `:yin.k/occurrence`, the lease state observed |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1266:## §7.10 Invariant compliance\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1268:| Invariant | How UCF honors it |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1270:| No hidden global state | Every dependency is declared in `:yin.k/requires` — *as computed by the declared fixed point, with its completeness stated* (`:yin.k/discovery`); the store travels as an explicit slice restored into an isolated store; fresh-name state and parked records travel explicitly; custody is facts on a named, possessed medium. |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1271:| No implicit control flow | Resume happens only at a safepoint the machine's parking transitions define; the successor chain is explicit `:yin.k/origin` links; the exporting state is an observed data state, never a notification. |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1272:| No callbacks | Lift and lower are step functions; custody is observed, never notified; a lapsed holder stops at its own bound; an unanswered proposal is a step status, not a wait. |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1273:| No shared mutable state | A UCF value is content-addressed and immutable; occurrence identity separates content variants from the one leased computation; two resumers of one value under `:fork` diverge into distinct incarnations; the isolated execution store shares nothing with the resumer's tasks. |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1274:| No layer collapsing | Canonicalize, encode, discover, arbitrate, load, restore, execute are separate functions with data between them. The engine's hot loop is untouched: lifting is a pure function over the blocked machine's value, and the exporting state is that value with an emptied wait-set and a retained record — driver discipline, not engine machinery. |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1275:| No assumed graphs | Sharing is an explicit value table keyed by address; cursor aliasing is an explicit cell graph, not inferred from positions; code refs are pcs relative to an addressed vector; nothing is resolved by pointer; foreign engines reconstruct dynamic state from the frame, never from layouts they assume. |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1286:## §7.11 Acceptance blockers for the implementation phase\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1350:### 7.11.1 Blocker-closure acceptance matrix\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1361:**Code identity (7.3; blocker 5).**\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1393:**Safepoint reconstruction (7.4; blocker 1).**\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1428:**Recursive portable encoding (7.5; blocker 2).**\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1457:**Ownership arbitration (7.7; blocker 4).**\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1482:**Dependency closure (7.6; blocker 3).**\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1:# yin.vm.code-as-tuples — code as content-addressed tuples\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:3:Status: Proposed, revision 8 (after the owner's 2026-09-15 clarification\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:36:## §1 Stance and layering\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:43:| Layer          | Example                        | What it holds                       | Identity           | Where it lives           | Mutability                     |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:45:| **Content**    | `{:type :lambda :params [x]…}`,| The Map AST code itself, stored as  | the content        | `dao.jing`, under its    | immutable; no `t`, no `m`, no  |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:46:|                | the Map AST semantic root      | a linearized bytecode of flat       | address — a row's  | address                  | name, no occurrence, no   