"`                              | walker `ast_walker.cljc:395`, codec `v2.cljc:444`, loader                   |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:343:|                                                    |                                     | `semantic.cljc:576`                                                         |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:345:| `:stream/make` buffer                              | `vm/default-stream-capacity` = 1024 | walker `ast_walker.cljc:439-440`, codec `v2.cljc:453`, loader               |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:346:|                                                    |                                     | `semantic.cljc:580-581`                                                     |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:348:| `:application` tail?                               | `false`                             | codec emits only `true` (`v2.cljc:412`); the linearizer reads `(boolean …)` |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:349:|                                                    |                                     | (`linearize.cljc:107-108`)                                                  |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:351:| `:application` / `:dao.stream.apply/call` operands | `[]`                                | walker `ast_walker.cljc:383`                                                |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:354:### 2.5 Exclusions, occurrences, and side tables\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:380:**Occurrences.** Content identity names *what*; three further things\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:427:| Side table             | Row                                                                                                                    | Keeper               |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:429:| source positions       | `[[:source medium batch j] root-address path file line col]`                                                           | the frontend that    |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:430:|                        |                                                                                                                        | parsed the file      |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:432:| frontend metadata      | `[origin root-address path key value]`                                                                                 | the frontend         |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:434:| instruction provenance | `[segment-address pc origin root-address path]`                                                                        | the lowering (§5.3)  |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:436:| macro declarations     | `[[:source medium batch j] path]`: the definition at `path` of the batch's `j`-th tree is a macro definition; inside   | the frontend,        |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:437:|                        | the batch envelope this is written `[j path :yin.macro/definition]` (§8.5)                                             | consumed by the      |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:438:|                        |                                                                                                                        | expander             |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:440:| harvest catalogue      | `[[:source medium batch] h j path]`: occurrence `[j path]` belongs to the `h`-th **original definition** in the        | the frontend or the  |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:441:|                        | batch's admission order, plain or macro; one original definition shared at several paths has several rows with one     | §9.1 adapter,        |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:442:|                        | `h`. The macro-only declaration ordinal `k` is derived from this table and the declarations, not stored (§8.5)         | consumed by the      |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:443:|                        |                                                                                                                        | expander             |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:446:### 2.6 A walker-local note on runtime mutation\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:465:## §3 The two boundary calls\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:467:### 3.1 `:vm/store-update` is excluded from the canonical grammar\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:507:### 3.2 `:stream/close` exists, in both codec and walker\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:528:## §4 Addressing\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:530:### 4.1 The grain\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:542:| Payoff                                        | How it works at the root-row grain                                                                                     |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:544:| `:yin.code/derived-from` as a content address | a derivation record naming the tree address as input and the segment address as output (§8.2) replaces the entity ref  |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:545:|                                               | of `v2.cljc:327` and `linearize.cljc:212`                                                                              |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:547:| the macro ledger                              | an expansion event naming input, output, and macro addresses (§8.4): expansion is a function from address to address,  |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:548:|                                               | and each attempt is its own event                                                                                      |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:550:| module manifests pinning AST content          | a manifest names the tree addresses it exports; equal content is equal address across hosts                            |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:552:| lowering as an address-to-address function    | `lower : tree → instruction vector`, and each application of it is one derivation record (§5.2)                        |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:561:### 4.2 The transitional encoder is inherited; ordinary identity use is unblocked\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:569:| Two different values                                   | Address today                       | Why it matters                                                           |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:571:| `[:literal [1 2]]` and `[:literal (1 2)]`              | distinct                            | `conj` appends to one and prepends to the other                          |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:573:| `[:literal [1 2]]` and `[:literal (seq [1 2])]`        | distinct                            | a seq is sequential but not a list, and both differ from the vector      |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:575:| `[:literal ^{:a 1} [1 2]]` and `[:literal ^{:a 2} [1   | distinct                            | `data` admits plain metadata (`linearize.cljc:58`) and programs may read |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:576:| 2]]`                                                   |                                      | it; collection metadata is now address-significant                      |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:606:### 4.3 Every node is addressed by construction\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:620:### 4.4 Sharing by content address replaces `:eid`; occurrences stay outside\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:639:**This structural collapse depends on the §4.2 encoder being injective, which it now is for ordinary values under default print bindings.** The three conformance pairs (vector/list, vector/seq, collection metadata) that used to make the encoder non-injective are closed; structurally distinct ordinary values no longer hash equal under the default host print configuration. The disclosed residuals remain gaps: scalar metadata and byte-array identity hashing need a future producer to matter here, but ambient print-var bindings reaching scalar bytes are live now — a row whose slots include scalars hashed inside such a binding is not covered by this collapse guarantee — see §4.2.\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:651:### 4.5 Free variables are queried, not tagged\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:708:**The row-only query is unsound, not just imprecise, when a name is free\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:742:**Not root-scoped as written — a real gap, not a hedge.** The test's\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:770:## §5 The segment level\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:772:### 5.1 The instruction vector is UCF §7.3.2\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:786:### 5.2 The hash chain is realized by derivation records\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:812:#### 5.2.1 The lowering profile\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:822:| Pinned by the profile                 | Reference value for `\\\"ast-to-bytecode\\\"`                                                                                                 |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:824:| input grammar                         | the §2 tuple grammar, by revision of this document                                                                             |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:826:| normalization applied before emission | saturation (§2.4), tail marks on `:application` only (§2.3), nothing else                                                      |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:828:| emission rules                        | the §5.3 flattening table of `yin.vm.semantic.md`, in the walker's evaluation order (operator, then operands left to right)    |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:830:| label and body order                  | labels numbered in emission order (`linearize.cljc:76-77`); bodies emitted after the main sequence, in the order lambdas were  |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:831:|                                       | encountered, including lambdas found inside bodies (`linearize.cljc:151-158`)                                                  |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:833:| terminators                           | main sequence ends in `:halt`, every body in `:return` (`linearize.cljc:150`, `:157`)                                          |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:835:| target execution contract             | the UCF §7.3.3 stamp the emitted grammar must satisfy                                                                          |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:846:#### 5.2.2 Verification, in two separate steps\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:869:### 5.3 Instruction provenance\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:888:## §6 Querying\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:890:### 6.1 The row relation and the two directions around it\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:904:**The Dedicated AST Indexer:** This row relation (called `$ast` in queries) is maintained by the dedicated AST indexer (§1). The indexer is a `dao.stream` observer peer to the evaluators (§7.1); its input is the row batches of §7.1; its output is this row relation plus the occurrence relation below; it is distinct from `dao.space.index`, which indexes datoms only (§6.5); it is a projection keeper per §1's Query layer, so discarding it loses nothing.\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:935:### 6.2 Segment rows\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:946:### 6.3 `q` over both, and the mechanics it rests on\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:986:### 6.4 Refs joined by address\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1006:### 6.5 What goes to the datom projection instead\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1015:| Query                                                                | Why the datom projection                                                                        |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1017:| attribute-dimension queries with the attribute unbound, `[?e ?a ?v]` | a flat row has no attribute slot; \\\"every fact about this node\\\" is an EAV question               |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1019:| `pull` and `entity-attrs` navigation (`query.cljc:715`, `:1481`)     | they navigate entity → attribute → value and reverse attrs                                      |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1021:| scale indexing under covered indexes (`dao.space.index`)             | the covered-index publisher and `open-published!` are EAVT/AEVT/AVET/VAET over datoms           |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1022:|                                                                      | (`query.cljc:452-476`)                                                                          |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1030:## §7 The VM around it\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1032:### 7.1 Load paths\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1039:| Evaluator            | Loader input         | What loading does                                                                                                        |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1041:| walker               | map AST              | natively reads map AST from stream topic without conversion — set `:program` and `:control` to the map.                    |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1042:|                      |                      |                                                                                                                          |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1043:|                      |                      |                                                                                                                          |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1045:| semantic             | instruction vector   | validate (§7.5), decode positional operands into the image (the `case` of `semantic.cljc:563-593` reading `(nth tuple i)`|\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1046:|                      |                      | instead of attribute maps), store under `:code` with the address as the alias column UCF §7.3.4 requires                 |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1048:| semantic,            | row set              | `lower` (§5.2) then the row above; composed by the composition exactly as `linearize/ast-loader` is today                |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1049:| AST medium           |                      | (`linearize.cljc:269-286`, chosen in `src/cljc/yin/repl/core.cljc:63-68`)                                             |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1059:### 7.2 Conformance: both paths, one validator, one image\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1061:**This section supersedes the sentence in UCF §7.3.4 that names the\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1099:### 7.3 Validation is the tuple grammar\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1107:### 7.4 Row rules\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1113:| Rule              | Defect when                                                                                                                                       |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1115:| `:tag`            | the element after the id is not a tag of §2.3                                                                                                     |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1117:| `:arity`          | the count differs from the tag's body arity plus one                                                                                              |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1119:| `:slot-kind`      | a slot's value is not of the slot's kind: a `node` slot that is not an address, a `nodes` slot that is not a vector of addresses, a `data` or     |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1120:|                   | `key` slot failing `plain-data?`, a `bool` slot that is not `true`/`false`, a `sym` slot that is not a symbol, a `syms` slot that is not a vector |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1121:|                   | of symbols                                                                                                                                        |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1123:| `:saturation`     | a saturated slot (§2.4) is nil                                                                                                                    |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1125:| `:id-resolves`    | a child id in a `node` or `nodes` slot names no row of the loaded set                                                                             |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1127:| `:acyclic`        | following child ids from a row revisits a row already on its own path                                                                             |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1129:| `:root-reachable` | a row of the loaded set is not reachable from the root row                                                                                        |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1143:### 7.5 Vector rules\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1151:| Rule             | Defect when                                                                                                                                         |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1153:| `:nonempty`      | the vector has no instructions, or the outer sequence is not a `vector?` — the canonical positional form (UCF §7.3.2), never a list                  |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1155:| `:mnemonic`      | the first element is not a mnemonic of `code/mnemonics` (`code.cljc:12-16`), or the element is not a `vector?` tuple — the same canonical-form rule  |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1157:| `:arity`         | the tuple's count differs from the mnemonic's arity in `yin.vm.semantic.md` §2.4 as saturated by UCF §7.3.2                                         |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1159:| `:operand-kind`  | an operand is not of its kind: `:const` and `:store-put` values or `:store-get`/`:store-put` keys fail `plain-data?` (the `key` kind of §2.2), a    |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1160:|                  | a `:var` name is not a symbol, a `:closure` params is not a vector of symbols, a `:ffi-call` op or `:resume` parked id is not a keyword, a `:gensym`  |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1161:|                  | prefix is not a string, a `:call` tail? is not exactly boolean, a `:stream-make` buffer is not a non-negative integer                                |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1163:| `:saturation`    | a saturated operand (`:gensym` prefix, `:stream-make` buffer, `:call` tail?, `:ffi-call` argc) is nil                                               |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1165:| `:target-bounds` | a `:jump`/`:branch-false` target or a `:closure` body is not an integer in `[0, length)`                                                            |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1167:| `:terminator`    | the last instruction is not in `code/terminators` (`code.cljc:19-21`)                                                                               |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1169:| `:argc`          | a `:call`/`:ffi-call` argc is not a non-negative integer                                                                                            |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1181:### 7.6 The hot loop never queries\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1192:### 7.7 Dependency closure is Datalog over the tuples\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1269:#### 7.7.1 Effect normalization: the footprint table\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:128