:1444:## §8 The ledger and refs\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1446:### 8.1 Two notations, one relation\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1466:| Logical slot | Persistent carrier                                                                                                                                      |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1468:| `t`          | the datom `t` the transactor stamped                                                                                                                    |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1470:| `op`         | for naming rows: the reserved validity marker in `m` (`:db/assert` 1, `:db/retract` 0); for every other op: the `:yin.ledger/op` value of a **ledger    |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1471:|              | event entity** (§8.2)                                                                                                                                   |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1473:| `address`    | a `v` slot                                                                                                                                              |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1475:| `ref`        | for naming rows: the local name entity in `e`; for address-to-address rows: a second `v` slot of the same event entity                                  |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1482:### 8.2 Ledger records and ledger events\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1489:| Op         | Record                                                | Meaning                                                                                           |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1491:| `:derive`  | `{:yin.ledger/op :derive :yin.ledger/input tree-addr  | `output` was computed from `input` by `function` under the lowering profile (§5.2.1)              |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1492:|            | :yin.ledger/output seg-addr :yin.ledger/function      |                                                                                                   |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1493:|            | fn-name :yin.ledger/profile profile-map}`             |                                                                                                   |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1495:| `:expand`  | `{:yin.ledger/op :expand :yin.ledger/input tree-in    | one expansion attempt; exactly one of `:yin.ledger/origin` (initial) and `:yin.ledger/parent`     |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1496:|            | :yin.ledger/call-root tree-in :yin.ledger/call-path   | (nested) is present; failures carry `:yin.ledger/error` instead of `:yin.ledger/output` (§8.4).   |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1497:|            | path :yin.ledger/origin [:source medium batch j]`     | `:yin.ledger/attempt` is the portable attempt identity of §8.4.1, scoped to the expander          |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1498:|            | **or** `:yin.ledger/parent parent-record-addr`        | incarnation, so two expanders or two executions of one expander observing one call never mint one |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1499:|            | `:yin.ledger/output tree-out :yin.ledger/macro        | record. The record holds no log-local id: a nested attempt names its parent by the parent's       |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1500:|            | lambda-addr :yin.ledger/attempt [incarnation          | record **address**, so the record is minted only after the parent's record exists                 |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1501:|            | counter]}`                                            |                                                                                                   |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1503:| `:publish` | `{:yin.ledger/op :publish :yin.ledger/subject         | a checkpoint occurrence was published as the UCF value at `output` (UCF §7.3.4)                   |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1504:|            | occurrence-id :yin.ledger/output ucf-addr}`           |                                                                                                   |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1557:### 8.3 Rows of the one relation\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1560:| Logical row                                   | Persistent form                                                                                                        |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1562:| `[t :assert tree-addr name]` — a name refers  | `[:db/add name :yin/code tree-addr]`                                                                                   |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1563:| to a tree                                     |                                                                                                                        |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1565:| `[t :retract tree-addr name]` — the name no   | `[:db/retract name :yin/code tree-addr]`, followed by the new assertion                                                |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1566:| longer does                                   |                                                                                                                        |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1568:| `[t :derive seg-addr tree-addr]` — a segment  | a `:derive` event entity (§8.2); direction: `input` is the tree, `output` is the segment                               |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1569:| was lowered from a tree                       |                                                                                                                        |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1571:| `[t :assert seg-addr k-occurrence]` — a       | `[:db/add occ :yin.k/segment seg-addr]` on the local occurrence entity                                                 |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1572:| segment is the address a continuation names   |                                                                                                                        |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1574:| `[t :expand tree-out tree-in]` — a tree is    | an `:expand` event entity (§8.4)                                                                                       |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1575:| the expansion of another                      |                                                                                                                        |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1577:| `[t :assert lambda-addr name]` under          | not a ledger row at all: macro-ness is an occurrence-bound declaration beside the tree (§8.5); the ledger records only |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1578:| `:yin.macro/definition`                       | the expander's harvest result, `[:db/add name :yin.macro/definition lambda-addr]`, for queries                         |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1580:| `[t :publish ucf-addr occurrence]` — a        | a `:publish` event entity; custody stays `dao.lease.md`'s vocabulary unchanged (UCF §7.7.2), keyed by the same local   |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1581:| checkpoint occurrence was published           | occurrence entity                                                                                                      |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1583:| `[t :assert tree-addr manifest]` — a module   | `[:db/add manifest :yin.module/exports tree-addr]`                                                                     |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1584:| manifest pins a tree                          |                                                                                                                        |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1592:### 8.4 Expansion events keep their identity\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1656:#### 8.4.1 Attempt identity is scoped to an expander incarnation\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1733:### 8.5 Macro declarations travel beside the tree\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1865:### 8.6 As-of queries are ledger views\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1906:## §9 Migration surface\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1908:### 9.1 The boundary, not a sweep\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1915:| Site                                             | Change                                                                                                              |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1917:| walker, `ast_walker.cljc`                        | Retains named variable evaluation (`:name`). `:lambda` arm binds by name. Does not use De Bruijn numbering. `:variable` arm (`:361-363`) is unchanged — still resolves through `resolve-var`'s env → store → primitives → modules fallthrough (§4.5). Closure application (`:191`, hot-path copies at `:511`/`:553`) changes from `(zipmap params args)` to nil-filling missing params. Adds `:stream/close` arm (§3.2).                                                                                                      |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1919:| loader, new                                      | validate rows (§7.4), reconstruct the map AST: `rows → map` (§6.1), the successor of `datoms->ast`                  |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1920:|                                                  | (`v2.cljc:494-559`) with content addresses in place of allocated ids                                                |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1922:| linearizer,                                      | reads the row relation through the same `get-attr`-over-an-index shape it has today (`lower-node`'s `(get-attr e    |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1923:| `linearize.cljc:87-148`,                         | :yin/type)` becomes a lookup by row id); `ast-children` becomes a table lookup of `node`/`nodes` slot positions;    |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1924:| `:230-242`                                       | `lower` takes a row set and returns a vector plus the §5.3 provenance table; emits `:var name` and `:closure params body`; `lower-ast` (`:245-252`) goes away     |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1926:| codec, `v2.cljc:372-559`                         | becomes `yin.vm/ast->semantic-bytecode`, the projection pair of §6.5 mapping Universal AST to Canonical Rows/Datoms.            |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1927:|                                                  | `:yin/root` and `:eid` removed; `:yin/address` added; retains `:yin/params` on lambda and `:yin/name` on variable |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1929:| `code/mnemonics`, `code/well-formed?`,           | `code/mnemonics` (`code.cljc:12-16`) is unchanged (§4.5). `well-formed?` keeps judging datom batches on the projection path before projection; the shared vector validator of §7.5 runs on   |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1930:| `code.cljc:12-180`                               | both paths after it                                                                                                 |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1932:| `semantic/load-image`,                           | decodes from the vector directly on the primary path; frame binding for `:closure` matches arguments to `params` by position, binding each to its name (§7.7.2); apply (`semantic.cljc:200`) changes from `zipmap` to nil-filling missing params; `:var` opcode is unchanged, resolving env → store → primitives → modules (§4.5); decodes the new operand (`:closure params body`); both paths call the §7.5 validator   |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1933:| `semantic.cljc:524-596`                          |                                                                                                                     |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1935:| frontends                                        | keep emitting map ASTs to the stream (as named universal ASTs). They do not perform the tuple projection. |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1936:| `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc`,                    | All projection to Semantic Tuples and side-tables is deferred to the Encoder Observer (`yin.vm/ast->semantic-bytecode`).        |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1937:| `python.cljc`, `php.cljc`                        |                                                                                                                     |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1938:|                                                  | never survive the boundary. The r7 adapter's ordering rules become the standing contract: first reject any `:macro? |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1939:|                                                  | true` lambda that is not the value operand of a `yin/def` as `:stray-macro-lambda`, then turn each admitted one into|\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1940:|                                                  | a declaration at its tree index and path, then strip the flag                                                       |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1942:| datom-batch adapter,                             | for media that carry datoms: derives `:yin/harvest` from entity order and entity identity while inlining, recording |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1943:| standing                                         | every `[j path]` at which each definition entity is emitted (the `datoms->ast` recursion, `v2.cljc:494-559`,        |\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1944:|                                                  | extended to carry the path and the